James inquired about the safety of cooking raw meatballs that had been refrigerated for a couple of days, noting a color change from reddish to brown. I explained that the color change could be due to oxidation but highlighted the importance of checking for off odors or sliminess as signs of spoilage. I clarified that raw ground meat typically lasts in the fridge for 1-2 days and advised caution, suggesting that if any doubts arose, it would be safer not to consume them. If the meatballs smelled fine and were not slimy, I recommended cooking them thoroughly to an internal temperature of 160°F (71°C) to eliminate any potential bacteria.
